Z||000003||Greg Piet||02-11-2001||01:41 PM||||Talking about losing to mustangs???<BR>Aww c'mon people  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>I pulled up next to a Ferrari a month or two ago and got SMOKED!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||lou_dias||02-11-2001||06:34 PM||||I have dubbed my car "Pony Killer" ever since I got my tricked out 3.4 OHV from the Fiero Factory.  None of them hang with me after 90 mph, however an LX from the late 80's with atleast an exhaust on it did sorta hand til 110.  Then I just kept going til about 130...  The LX's are known to be lighter that the GT's (kinda like a formula).<P>I do circle track racing over the summer and it was pathetic what I did to a top mustang off the line. I got 2 lenghts in front of him and got right in front of him before the first turn.  It's a 1/3 mile track and you start half way up one of the straightaways.<P>The problem with 5 speed mustangs is that their 5th gear is too low.  After 4th they have nothing.||||reg||1
Z||000005||firstfiero||02-11-2001||07:15 PM||||   sounds like my fiero...if I don't have you by the end of 3rd I'm toast. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Formula88||02-11-2001||09:39 PM||||Hey, lou, how's that 3.4 run?  Got any performance numbers for us?  Always looking for more data on the inevitable engine swap.  My 2.8 won't last forever.... hopefully long enough to afford the new engine, though... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||lou_dias||02-12-2001||09:28 AM||||It dynoed at 150hp at the wheels and 204 ft*lbs of torque, but I would call that on a bad day.  It just performs stronger than how it was running when I dynoed it most of the time.  It's the torque that let's me muscle past anybody after 110mph cause I got enough of it to keep my car moving.<P>Mods:<BR>rebuilt 3.4 from Fiero Factory<BR>ported heads & intake from Associated Auto<BR>1.52 roller rockers<BR>Crane Compucam w/double springs<BR>TRW high-strength pushrods<BR>adjustable fuel pressure regulator @44psi<BR>K&N air filter, Accel coil, Bosch 4-way platinum wires<BR>Sprint F1 enamel coated headers<BR>Hollow Cat conv, IRM dual exhaust(no muffler)<BR>heads cleaned/shaved a few times<BR>SI valves<P>things I still need to do:<BR>bigger bore Throttle body<BR>Alumninum flywheel<BR>TURBO!!!!!!!!!!!!!<BR>pulleys (don't think I want this one)<BR>Ram-air setup since I removed the airbox||||reg||1
Z||000008||DL10||02-12-2001||09:50 PM||||Light um up.......Lets Race<P>------------------<BR> DL10 Predator      <IMG SRC="http://chicagolandreplicar.tripod.com/images/lc_db1.gif">   <BR>   <A HREF="mailto:dbagwell1@Prodigy.net">dbagwell1@Prodigy.net</A>     <A HREF="http://pages.prodigy.net/dbagwell1" TARGET=_blank>http://pages.prodigy.net/dbagwell1</A>||||reg||1
