Z||000010||filthyscarecrow||02-13-2001||01:05 AM||||well, i said earlier that my integra was faster than my SE V-6. don't get me wrong, the SE isnt' slow. the guy in the 750 BMW found that out the hard way when i passed him goin up the big hill on the front straight at elkhart lake. so did the guy in the 944 on the hill up to turn 6. and the guy in the corvette coming out of the carousel (this was due more to exit speed though. i had 20mph on him. his tires were screeching, mine weren't). but i guarantee the integra can beat it to 75mph. don't get me wrong, i would never give up the fiero, but i would love to put that B18C5(typeR) engine in the back of it...<BR>  i'm hoping to take both to the track this summer and see what they can do... <BR>and i gotta admit though, the honda engine sounds better at 6000rpm than the fiero does anywhere in the rev band. i don't know where they get the idea that hondas buzz. mine sounds like a race car. it sounds a lot like the older formula one cars when they didn't scream so high...<BR>  i guess i figure why stick to one car when they're both a lot of fun...?||||reg||1
Z||000011||ur2biteme||02-13-2001||06:52 PM||||well, the thing i've noticed about the "ricers" driving the integras and such that get burned by everything under the sun is that they shift too early.  i've raced an integra before with my 4 banger and won.  he looked like he was shifting at around 4500 or something.  then again, my best friend has a 97 rs that's bone stock.  he whipped my a$$ because he knows how to drive it. <P>i'd gamble as to say that a well worked quad 4 could put out considerably more power than the type R engine.  it has more displacement.  my opinion and experiences have brought me to the conclusion that VTEC is overrated.  it's a good help, but the saying holds true even in the 4 cylinder battle: there is no replacement for displacement. <P>------------------<BR>Bob's '87 econo coupe<BR>aproaching 171k :)<BR> <A HREF="http://members.fortunecity.com/ur2biteme" TARGET=_blank>a little piece of my madness</A>||||reg||1
Z||000012||filthyscarecrow||02-13-2001||10:44 PM||||you're probably right in that a well worked quad 4 could put out more power than a B18C5, but i'm also thinking reliability. quad 4's aren't exactly the posterchild for a reliable engine. i remember reading somewhere that head gasket failure was as high as 20%<BR>as for the shifting thing, hell ya, you can't expect to beat much if you're shifting at 4500 rpm. but you can beat quite a few people if yuo're shifting just before the rev limiter kicks in. and the cool thing is that you can rev a honda that high on a fairly regualr basis and it can take the abuse. most american engines can't. my friend had the V-6 in his 86GT rebuilt (he's known for revving the piss out of cars) and only months later he was ready for a rebuild. <BR>and there is a replacement for displacement: RPM. <BR>formula one engines are 3.0 litres, yet make over 800hp. why? because they spin to almost 20,000 rpm. CART engines make over 900hp out of a 2.65L v-8. how? they are turbocharged, but mildly so. they run under 5lbs of boost, but they spin to 16,000 rpm and thus they move a scheitload of air, and with that, fuel. horsepower is all about moving air. there are several replacements for displacements, rpm, forced induction, nitrous (moves more oxygen). and call it my 2 cents, but i think high revving engines sound better and are more fun to drive. <BR>my little 1.8 L puts out more power at the wheels than my friend's 2L eclipse. and the same if not more than my 2.8 fiero. sure one is DOHC and the other is from the early 80's, but the v-6 is bigger and less powerful. honestly, i have no problem with rice cars. i like anything that's well engineered (and as far as i'm concerned, the fiero is the best engineered car america has ever produced, but there are better cars out there, and japan just happens to have produced some of them), even if it might annoy some people. some of them are even pretty impressive, like the NSX or the integra typeR. but come on, 200hp out of 1.8L! that's over 100hp/liter. and 8500rpm to play with... tell me that's not fun!<BR><P>------------------<BR>allow me to show you my exhaust pipes...||||reg||1
Z||000013||danny boy||02-13-2001||11:17 PM|||| Hey firstfiero, Come on down the road to Morgantown, I'll show you a "ricer" you'll lose to. <BR>   If Japanese cars are rice burners does that make German cars Jew burners? Think about it before you say it.||||reg||1
