Z||000015||firstfiero||02-14-2001||09:25 AM||||    Germans make some of the finest cars produced. I love bmw and Porsche and have owned both! When I use the term ricer it is for the little stupid kid (probobly like you) who pulls up next to me in a honda 4 banker with nothing but stickers,a big respoiler, and a big exhaust and now think their fast. THAT IS A RICER!!! As a whole I don't have a problem with jap. cars. I like mr2's alot. If you fit into the above mentioned description...come on down!  ||||reg||8
Z||000016||ThatRickGuy||02-14-2001||10:33 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by filthyscarecrow:<BR><B>and there is a replacement for displacement: RPM. <BR>formula one engines are 3.0 litres, yet make over 800hp. why? because they spin to almost 20,000 rpm. CART engines make over 900hp out of a 2.65L v-8. how? they are turbocharged, but mildly so. they run under 5lbs of boost, but they spin to 16,000 rpm and thus they move a scheitload of air, and with that, fuel. horsepower is all about moving air.  some of them are even pretty impressive, like the NSX or the integra typeR. but come on, 200hp out of 1.8L! that's over 100hp/liter. and 8500rpm to play with... tell me that's not fun!<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes, but have you ever driven a stick shift car that has that kinda RPM band in rush hour traffic? If we wanted all out powered, we would build up our V-6's to spin that fast, yes it is possible. The problem being I-95 north bound just south of DC for 50 on weekday mornings. Do you really want to rev up to 4000 rpms just to move your car 10 feet? My fiero might not be as fast as those high revers, but I've never had one of them take me off the line, top end tho, I'd be blown away. But my Fiero is versitle, I can luanch off a line, I can cruise comfy at 80mph, and I can wade threw stop and go traffic with out risking ankle strain. :P<P>||||reg||1
